{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 complete — RED→GREEN, kill matrix, replication\n\n### Fix\nThird fail-closed seam in `scripts/gen_env_registry.py`: `StaleEnvReadHelperRow`, raised by\n`_raise_for_stale_rows()` from `scan()` when any `KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` row names a helper with\nno `def`/`async def` under the shipped scan root. All stale rows are reported at once, each\nwith its declared `(pos, prefix)`. The four ghost rows are removed; `docs/env-vars.md` is\nregenerated.\n\n**Root-independent by design and documented as such:** `_shipped_function_names()` resolves\nagainst `DEFAULT_SCAN_ROOT`, never against `scan`'s `root` argument. Measured reason: against\na one-module synthetic tree 13 of 13 rows look stale, so a root-scoped check would abort all\n11 `_scan_source` tests in `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py`. Same pattern as\n`check_config_ownership._check_registry_completeness` / `_validate_exceptions`.\n\n**Validate-and-fail only.** The seam refuses and names the rows; it does not prune or infer\nthem. The exception docstring records why: auto-pruning would silently discard a row whose\nhelper was merely renamed — the exact case worth surfacing.\n\n`scan()` keeps its 2-tuple arity. File is 583 LOC (cap 800); complexity ratchet\n`active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0`.\n\n### RED → GREEN\nOracle: `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py`, three tests, **written and observed RED before\nany fix existed**, then **held out of the fix subagent's working tree** (moved aside, path\ndeclared off-limits; the fixer never opened it).\n\n| test | RED evidence, pre-fix |\n|---|---|\n| `test_every_known_env_helper_row_has_a_live_definition` (census) | `['_env_int', '_int_pref', '_rebar_env', '_str_pref'] == []` |\n| `test_stale_known_env_helper_row_aborts_the_scan` (gate) | `Failed: DID NOT RAISE RuntimeError` |\n| `test_a_partial_scan_root_does_not_flag_every_row_as_stale` (FP control) | passes both ways by design |\n\nBoth failures are real assertion failures, not import/fixture errors. Post-fix: 24 passed.\nGating proof — collected: yes · executed (not SKIP/XFAIL): yes · gate: `make test`\n(`pytest -m \"not integration and not external\"`), which covers `tests/unit`.\n\n**The census is not tautological.** It derives the table side from `gen.KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS`\nand the tree side from its **own** `ast` walk (`_defined_function_names`), never from the\nimplementation's `_shipped_function_names`. That independence is what the kill matrix proves.\n\n### Kill matrix — 4/4 killed, each side mutated independently\n\n| # | side | mutation | result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| M1 | validator | early-`return` in `_raise_for_stale_rows` | **RED** — gate test: `DID NOT RAISE RuntimeError` |\n| M2 | validator | scope the check to the caller's `root` instead of `DEFAULT_SCAN_ROOT` | **RED** — FP control: `StaleEnvReadHelperRow` on a temp dir |\n| M3 | **table** | re-add `\"_str_pref\": (0, \"\")` | **RED** — census: `['_str_pref'] are KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS rows with no definition` |\n| M4 | **tree** | rename `_severities_env` → `_severities_pref` (def **and** its call site — the faithful `269b4d5678` replay), leaving the row | **RED** — census: `['_severities_env'] ...` |\n\nNo survivors, so no equivalent-mutant argument is needed. M3 moves only the table and M4\nmoves only the tree, and each turns the census RED on its own — the tautology the brief warned\nabout (both sides moving together) is ruled out by construction.\n\nA first attempt at M4 renamed `_gate_str_pref`, which broke an unrelated import and produced a\n**collection error rather than an assertion failure** — inconclusive, not a kill. It was\nre-run as M4 above against a helper with no cross-module callers. Recording that because a\ncollection error is easy to misread as a successful kill.\n\n**Refactoring litmus:** every assertion is on observable output (the table's contents vs. the\ntree's definitions; a raised exception and its message text). None asserts a private name, an\nintermediate variable, or a grep of source, so a behaviour-preserving rename inside the\ngenerator does not turn them red.\n\n### Step 6 — original report no longer reproduces\nCensus on the fixed tree: **9 rows, 0 ghosts**. Draining a live helper now yields\n`gen_env_registry.py --check` **exit 1** (was exit 0, silent) with:\n`stale KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS row(s) — no function of this name is defined under src/rebar/ ... - _severities_env (row: (0, ''))`.\nArtifact intact: `_164 variables._` before and after; line 9 now lists exactly the 9 live\nhelpers. The fixer independently confirmed `_int_pref('SOME_KNOB')` now produces\n`unresolved-env-read below approved seam`, identical to the `_mystery_pref` control — harm H3\nis closed.\n\n### A Phase-1 claim I had to retract\nThe plan asserted the new seam would transitively protect `check_config_ownership.py` because\nthat gate calls `scan()`. **It does not.** Its only `scan()` call is in `derive_env_baseline`\n(`:161`), which has **zero callers repo-wide**; `check()` is\n`_validate_exceptions + _check_registry_completeness + _scan_files`. Measured: with a row\ndeliberately stale, `gen_env_registry.py --check` exits 1 while `check_config_ownership.py`\nexits **0**. The ownership gate's real exposure was the ghost rows themselves, which are\nremoved; recurrence is gated portably by the drift gate and the census test under `make test`.\nFiled as `teary-thistle-solitaire` (2a3e). The commit message was corrected to drop the false\nclaim.\n\n### Step 7 — sibling sweep\n\n**Axis 1 (construct: a name-keyed registry consumed by name, with no existence check against\nthe tree).** Swept the adjacent registries; **no live siblings**:\n- `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` — `_validate_exceptions()` is structural only (glob / `.py` suffix /\n  non-empty rationale), with **no** path-or-symbol existence check. Same class, but the table\n  is **empty** (0 rows) after RP-04 drained it, so there is no instance to fix. Accepted.\n- `_CREDENTIAL_BOUNDARY_RELPATHS` — 4/4 exist, and a stale entry fails in the *safe*\n  direction (it shrinks `read_names`, producing MORE `UNOWNED` findings). Not the defect.\n- `rebar._deprecations.REGISTRY` (env channel) vs `config._LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES` — 7/7 in both\n  directions, zero phantoms. Clean.\n- `KEY_BEARING_ENVIRON_ATTRS` / `BULK_ENVIRON_ATTRS` — stdlib attribute names, not tree\n  symbols. N/A.\nBounded: this swept the registries reachable from the two config gates, not every table in the\nrepo.\n\n**Axis 2 (parity census).** Rule, stated without naming the fixed site: *a registry row keyed\nby a symbol name must correspond to a real definition in the tree.*\n1. CLI command — **N/A**, `KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` has no CLI surface.\n2. MCP/API tool — **N/A**, not exposed.\n3. Library facade — **N/A**, `scripts/` is not importable as `rebar.*`.\n4. Automated callers — `scripts/check_config_ownership.py` imports the table and uses it by\n   name at `:430`/`:440`/`:451`. **Covered, but not by the raise** (see the retraction above):\n   covered by the ghost removal now, and against recurrence by the CI drift gate plus the\n   census test. Disposition: fixed in scope, with the residual coupling ticketed as 2a3e.\n5. Dual direction — the mirror (tree → table) already fails closed via\n   `UnregisteredEnvReadHelper` (change 1990). **Both directions are now closed**; that is the\n   parity completion this change delivers.\n\n### Residual risk & prevention\n- **`derive_env_baseline` is dead code in a CI gate script** — *ticket filed*:\n  `teary-thistle-solitaire` (2a3e-e022-1f80-4c5f), linked `discovered_from`.\n- **The `prefix` field now has zero live users and zero live coverage** (`_rebar_env` was its\n  only user). The heldout fixture now asserts `prefix + \"SOME_KNOB\"`, but with every live\n  prefix empty that assertion is vacuous — *ticket filed*: `material-sciophilic-echidna`\n  (3a57-82b0-74bb-44e8), linked `discovered_from`.\n- **`tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py:31` carried a comment attributing\n  `REBAR_RECONCILER_VERBOSE` to the `_rebar_env` REBAR_ prefix path**, which has not existed\n  since `d361eb28e4` — the assertion had been passing for a different reason than it claimed —\n  *fixed in scope* (comment corrected to state the current path).\n- **`LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` has no existence validation** — *accepted*: the table is empty, so\n  there is nothing to fix today and a speculative guard is not worth a change.\n- **`_shipped_function_names` is `lru_cache`d for the process lifetime** — *accepted*:\n  `main()` runs once per process and no caller mutates `src/rebar` mid-process; the cache is\n  what keeps the check off the hot path of the 11 synthetic-tree scans.\n\n### Fix-safety audit\n- **Restoration, not creation** — the seam enforces an invariant the table already asserted\n  (`gen_env_registry.py:134`, \"Signatures verified against the current tree\") and that\n  `c1f17861ec`'s own commit message promised (\"no phantom rows\"). No new CLI command, no new\n  user-visible artifact, no new mutating external call.\n- **No new dependency** — the only added imports are `functools` and `ast`, both stdlib and\n  both already used in this codebase.\n- **No test weakening** — the whole diff contains exactly **one** deletion in a pre-existing\n  test file: the stale comment above. The heldout fixture change keeps\n  `assert len(errors) == 1` and tightens `\"SOME_KNOB\" in errors[0]` to\n  `prefix + \"SOME_KNOB\" in errors[0]`; nothing removed, nothing vaguer, no skip/xfail.\n\n### Gates run before push\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `make lint` | **exit 0** — ruff check + format-check; complexity ratchet `active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0`; and, because they live inside `make lint` (`Makefile:215,221`), both repo-wide oracles: `check_config_ownership.py` and `gen_env_registry.py --check` |\n| `make typecheck` | **Success**, mypy, 617 source files |\n| `tests/scripts` (full tier) | **1047 passed, 2 skipped** |\n| every test referencing `gen_env_registry` / `KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` / `env-vars.md` — 12 files across `tests/unit`, `tests/scripts`, `tests/interfaces` | **239 passed** |\n| `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py` | **24 passed** |\n\n**Full-suite caveat, stated plainly:** a complete `make test` did **not** finish locally. This\nhost is shared and other sessions were running their own sweeps throughout (load average 22-24\non 18 cores; two foreign `pytest tests/unit` processes observed), so every full run was either\nstarved past the tool's 10-minute cap or killed. I ran the 12 files that reference the changed\nsurface instead, plus the whole `tests/scripts` tier, all green. The complete suite is what the\nGerrit `Verified` gate runs on a dedicated runner, and per AGENTS.md this ticket stays open\nuntil that vote is green — a passing completion-verifier is not a substitute.\n\nNote the `1 error` in the pre-change baseline sweep\n(`test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py`: \"New entries appeared in REPO_ROOT\") was\nself-inflicted — my own concurrent `rebar review-plan` wrote a `.rebar/usage…` log into\nREPO_ROOT mid-run. It is not a defect and not caused by this change.\n\n### A deliberate omission\n`docs/env-vars.md:5` still says the scan is \"fail-closed on **both halves**\". There are now\nthree seams, but that sentence is about *read* coverage (the `os.environ` half and the helper\nhalf), which is still accurate — the new seam guards the table, not a read half. Rewriting the\nprose would grow the generated-artifact diff beyond the mechanism under proof, so it was left\nalone rather than changed silently.\n\n### Landed for review\n**Gerrit change 1999** — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1999\ncommit `d384b91f8b`, `Change-Id: I0145c504f0aadbec480c2caf993fed1ebb8f9d1e`,\n`rebar-ticket: 84c7-486f-9a13-4c3f`, DCO signed-off.\nDiff: 4 files, +183 -13 — `scripts/gen_env_registry.py` (+84), `docs/env-vars.md` (1 line),\n`tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py` (+100), `tests/scripts/test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py` (+7 -3).\n\n**Ticket stays `in_progress` until 1999 has `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` and merges.**\nOn close, use `--class=preexisting --caused-by=0f21-ca03-f063-4562`."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787317379985676001,"uuid":"8c3c8ad1-a588-439f-8a8b-c00e8d7807b5"}